#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# beta

#% text
# `beta(a, b)` gives the beta function `gamma(a)*gamma(b)/gamma(a + b)`.

#% text
# `beta(z, a, b)` gives the incomplete beta function, the integral of `t^(a - 1)*(1 - t)^(b - 1)` for `t` from 0 to `z`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# The complete function is DLMF 5.12.1, the incomplete one DLMF 8.17.1; `beta(1, a, b)` is `beta(a, b)`.

#% item
# Rational arguments for which the gamma functions are exact give exact values; machine numbers and balls give numerical values. Symbolic arguments stay unevaluated.

#% item
# `beta` is listable.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
beta(2, 3)
#% output
#= 1/12

#% cell
beta(1/2, 1/2)
#% output
#= pi

#% cell
beta(2.5, 1.5)
#% output
#= 0.19634954084936207

#% text
# The incomplete function:

#% cell
beta(0.5, 2.0, 3.0)
#% output
#= 0.057291666666666664

#% subsection
# Scope

#% text
# 30 digits:

#% cell
n(beta(1/3, 2/3), 30)
#% output
#= 3.627598728468435701188156515284311

#% text
# The incomplete function at several points:

#% cell
beta([0.25, 0.5, 0.75], 2.0, 2.0)
#% output
#= [0.026041666666666668, 0.08333333333333333, 0.140625]

#% subsection
# Properties and relations

#% text
# The integral definition:

#% cell
n_integrate(t^1.5*(1 - t)^0.5, [t, 0, 1]) - beta(2.5, 1.5)
#% output
#= -5.551115123125783e-17

#% text
# The regularized form divides by the complete function:

#% cell
beta(0.3, 2.0, 3.0)/beta(2.0, 3.0) - beta_regularized(0.3, 2.0, 3.0)
#% output
#= 0.0

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `gamma`, `beta_regularized`, `inverse_beta_regularized`, `binomial`
